+The right sides are direct images of relations.
+
+To construct these data, factor $f\wedge g:A\wedge A\to B\wedge B$
+by induction on the number of $\eta_p$ and $\epsilon_p$
+constructors. Extracting an $\eta_p$ adds $\neg p\vee p$ as a
+conjunct at the source; extracting an $\epsilon_p$ adds
+$p\wedge\neg p$ as a disjunct at the target. Each step removes
+one such constructor from the middle term, leaving a positive
+middle term when the induction terminates. Extend the diagonal
+$\Delta_A:A\to A\wedge A$ and the projections
+$\pi_i^{B,B}:B\wedge B\to B$, for $i=1,2$, by identities on
+the added formulas. Composing with these extensions gives two
+positive terms with source $A'$ and target $B'$; naturality of
+the extracted prefixes and suffixes gives the common morphisms
+$u$ and $v$. Finally, precompose and postcompose these terms
+with endomorphisms of $A'$ and $B'$ formed from $1_A$ and
+$1_B$, respectively, and zero endomorphisms on the added
+conjunction factors and disjunction summands.
+These endomorphisms preserve the factorizations and give the
+displayed direct-image relations.
+
+Thus equality of $G[f]$ and $G[g]$ gives equality of the middle relations.
 Positive coherence equates $[f_0]$ and $[g_0]$, and the
